  "notices": [
   {
    "scope": "resolution",
    "text": "Depth pooled into 13 layer groups (5.5.5.5.4.4.4.4.4.4.4.4.4) at the native layers' stored edges: each group bin holds the width-weighted mean of its layers' densities, the exact area-weighted overlap of the native layers, so no bin exceeds the per-layer peak and the energy is conserved. The selection's ρ_ref, the colour scale and the floor counts are the pooled grid's; a dataset reference stays the per-layer peak, which bounds the pooled values too. The comb is still measured on the raw accumulation grid."
   },
   {
    "scope": "frame",
    "text": "Per-shower translated frame: 2 event(s), 4 showers superimposed at their own entry points. ⟨ρ⟩ is energy per event and per mm², so it sums both showers of an event."
   },
   {
    "scope": "frame",
    "text": "No cell-footprint comb measured on the raw per-shower translated accumulation grid, before any display smoothing (worst lag-1 per axis: Δx +0.06, Δy −0.10); each cell's footprint is integrated exactly by area-weighted box overlap."
   },
   {
    "scope": "frame",
    "text": "Bins below 10⁻³ of ρ_ref are not drawn (ΔxΔy 312 bins holding 0.178% of its in-window energy; ΔyΔz 177 bins holding 0.332% of its in-window energy; ΔxΔz 134 bins holding 0.2% of its in-window energy), so the outer edge of the colour is the display floor, not the edge of the shower. Bins with no energy at all are empty."
   },
   {
    "scope": "frame",
    "text": "Colours are relative to this selection's own peak density on the raw 20 mm accumulation grid (stated in the panel's Details drawer), which the displayed field never exceeds; switch the density normalisation to the dataset peak to compare colours across selections."
   },
   {
    "scope": "frame",
    "text": "With 2 event(s) the fitted display ranges and the mean centroids rest on weak evidence and are labelled provisional."
   }
  ]
